# Lab 6: Observability
# Health endpoints are public: no token needed.
@host = https://localhost:7001

### Full health report (JSON after Lab 6)
GET {{host}}/health

### Liveness: is the process up? (ignores dependencies)
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness: can it serve traffic? (checks the store)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Make the store slow: /health goes Degraded, still 200
PUT {{host}}/dev/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 700, "errorRate": 0, "available": true }

### Take the store down: /health and /health/ready go 503, /health/live stays 200
PUT {{host}}/dev/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 0, "errorRate": 0, "available": false }

### Back to normal
POST {{host}}/dev/chaos/reset

### Trigger an error, copy the traceId, and find it in the console log
GET {{host}}/dev/boom

### Recent traces (what the lab client's trace panel draws)
GET {{host}}/dev/traces
